  "summary": "The North Liberty, Iowa City Council voted 3-1 to end its contract with Flock, which operated 12 license-plate reading cameras at a cost of about $36,000 per year. The city plans to turn off data sharing immediately, though physical cameras may remain while contract requirements are worked out.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The North Liberty City Council voted 3-1 Tuesday night to end its contract with Flock.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "The city plans to turn off data sharing Wednesday, meaning North Liberty will no longer share data with other agencies or access data from their systems",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "reducing data retention from 30 days to seven days and limiting which outside agencies can access the system",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    }
